## Session summary

**Criterion NOT met** — `cache_coherency` still fails; marker NOT written. Build `DF34891E` compiles cleanly but is **not yet deployed/tested** (relay boundary hit).

### Refuted (RULE 4)
The approved sess117 "hard cache-barrier step 1" — generalizing the AG-meta release-side evict from bnobt/cntbt to **all** AG-meta (agf/agi/inobt/finobt) — **reintroduced the bnobt double-free corruption** (`ltbno+ltlen>bno` shutdown) plus a 129s rename. Evicting AGF desyncs its cached freeblks/longest/btree-root from the bnobt leaves. **Reverted.** Also confirmed the acquire-side `mxfs_dlm_invalidate_ag_meta` *already* invalidates all AG-meta comprehensively — so AG-meta is not the residual blocker.

### Proven root of the corruption-shutdown→barrier-stall→timeout
The shutdown is `xfs_dialloc` → EFSCORRUPTED (badmagic) → `xfs_trans_cancel` on a dirty trans → FS shutdown, which hangs peers on the test barrier. It's **downstream of INODE RESURRECTION**: xfsaild's `xfs_iflush` copies a live in-core inode over a peer-freed on-disk dinode (proven via the sess102 `P-IRESURRECT` detector firing on comm=xfsaild immediately before each dialloc badmagic). Mutual exclusion holds (P106-STALE-EX=0); read-side coherency is fine — it's the xfsaild **write-side**.

### Fix implemented (Gemini RULE-5 validated)
Added `MXFS_IF_FIRST_FLUSH` in-core flag (set on `XFS_IGET_CREATE`, cleared on first flush) so `xfs_iflush` can reliably distinguish a legitimate new-inode first flush from a resurrection ghost — necessary because XFS `di_gen` is **random** (chunk-init vs per-alloc prandom), which defeated every gen-comparison discriminator I tried (each false-positived on new inodes → "cannot see <file>" + AIL stall). Guard: skip the disk copy when `!FIRST_FLUSH && disk_gen != incore_gen`.

### Key verified signal
On the interim build, the resurrection guard **eliminated the corruption** (`shutdown=0, ltbno=0` on all nodes — previously a node always crashed). The flag fix removes the only remaining regression (new-inode false positives).

### Next session
Deploy `DF34891E` (virsh destroy+start all 4 → reset4 → run cache_coherency ×3); expect no shutdown and cross_visibility restored. If a *visibility* residual remains without shutdown, that's the separate dir-block lost-update half. Full detail in memory `sess118_lessons`.

